      "Most planners solve this by hiring entertainment for one part of the evening and hoping the rest takes care of itself. A DJ plays background music. A volunteer introduces the speakers. The event coordinator whispers cues from the wings. It works. Sort of. But 'sort of' isn't what your clients are paying for. (We explore this further in <a href='/blog/entertainment-gap-planners-dont-know'>The Entertainment Gap Most Planners Don't Know They Have</a>.)",
