      "Think about it from the guest's perspective. During cocktails, a charismatic performer blows their mind with close-up magic. They're laughing, they're amazed, they're telling their friends. Then that same person takes the stage, welcomes everyone, and guides them through the rest of the evening. There's no cold introduction. No 'who is this person?' moment. The MC is already everybody's favorite person in the room.",
      "This matters more than most planners realize. The number one complaint guests have about events isn't the food, the venue, or the entertainment. It's pacing. Events that run long. Speeches that start late. Transitions that feel clunky. An experienced MC prevents all of this because managing energy and timing is literally the job.",
